From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: novatek-nt36523: add the Lenovo TB320FC NT36523N

The Lenovo Legion Y700 Gen2 (TB320FC, SM8475) drives a bonded dual-DSI
Novatek NT36523N: 1600x2560 FHD+ as two 800-wide C-PHY links in video
burst mode, compressed with DSC 1.2 (8 bpc, one 800x20 slice per link,
block prediction on).  The link runs at the vendor's verified
~573.5 MHz pixel clock rather than the uncompressed
htotal x vtotal x framerate rate.

The init sequence is the bootloader's qcom,mdss-dsi-on-command for the
144 Hz "hyper" variant, decoded out of the vendor devicetree; the two
vendor settle delays (100 ms / 10 ms) ride with the final sleep-out
handoff.  The reset line is declared active-low in the devicetree so the
driver's built-in sequence lands in the vendor's low-to-high physical
order, as on the elish and baldur panels.

NOT TESTED ON HARDWARE.  The device has not been booted with a mainline
kernel yet; this is written from the vendor devicetree, no more.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-novatek-nt36523.c
@@ -1443,6 +1443,614 @@
 	.is_dual_dsi = true,
 };
 
